### 1a: a bucket that does not exist (the key is limited to hs-lifecycle-test)
bob@rcbox:~$ time sudo hotserve-backup setup b2:hs-rc-no-such-bucket-7f3a:
account hotserve-backup: present
a run would back up demo, under /var/lib/liveswap
Storage key id (B2_ACCOUNT_ID): <keyID>
Storage secret key (B2_ACCOUNT_KEY): 
looking for a repository at b2:hs-rc-no-such-bucket-7f3a: (up to 10s)
no repository answered within 10s: a bucket not made yet, a wrong key and a wrong host look alike here; a new repository will be made with the password shown next
Repository password (new): <52 characters>
Store it off the box now, with the repository URL, b2:hs-rc-no-such-bucket-7f3a:, and the storage key: with those three, `restic -r <url>` reads every backup from any machine; without the password nothing can.
Type stored to go on: stored
restic could not make or open the repository (exit 1): Fatal: create repository at b2:hs-rc-no-such-bucket-7f3a: failed: Fatal: unable to open repository at b2:hs-rc-no-such-bucket-7f3a:: NewBucket: b2_list_buckets: 401:
the storage refused the key, or could not be reached: the key id and secret again (the password shown above still applies)
